+# Layered flexible assemblies
+
+MechanicalIR optionally declares `layered_assemblies`. Each stack names an existing
+host occurrence, a CAD frame, an outward normal, an in-plane material direction,
+ordered physical layer occurrences and joins between adjacent layers. Layer IDs
+and join IDs are composition entities, distinct from physical component IDs.
+Thickness is a nominal declaration; null means unknown. `inspect_layers` sums only
+complete declarations. It does not check CAD thickness or solve deformation.
+
+MechanicalPart optionally declares `flexibility`: directional elastic moduli,
+bending rigidities, strain limits, minimum bend radius and pinned material evidence.
+Absent properties remain unknown. Warp/weft identify local material axes; isotropy,
+cloth behavior and measured material performance are never inferred.
+
+ElectricalPart.engineering optionally declares `temperature_sensor` and
+`conductor_response`. These describe measurement roles, calibration and response
+coefficients. They do not produce readings or evaluate resistance changes. Geometry,
+material strain and thermal states retain their existing domain owners.
+
+## Composition relationships
+
+| Relationship | Source | Target |
+|---|---|---|
+| mounted_on_layer | Whole electrical component | Mechanical layer |
+| thermal_representation | Whole mechanical component or layer | Thermal node |
+| observes_temperature | Electrical component with typed temperature sensor role | Thermal node |
+| wearer_contact | Segment-bound HumanIR mechanical contact port | Exposed contact-role layer |
+| thermal_contact | Segment-bound HumanIR thermal exchange port | Thermal node heat port |
+
+Use existing `same_object` for shared physical component views and `thermal_source`
+for electrical heat loads. Endpoints retain revision/digest checks. Validation
+checks endpoint meaning, not physical contact, circuit routing or heat transfer.
+An aggregate host need not be an additional solid or mass. Do not count both a
+module envelope and its sublayers as separate mass without a mass allocation.
+
+These are additive optional fields on the native 1.0 schema. Legacy payloads omit
+the new defaults, preserving normalization and hashes. Older readers cannot consume
+populated extensions without updating. Legacy projection reports layered/material
+facts as unrepresentable rather than silently discarding them. Schema discovery
+uses the existing domain registry; no TextileIR or separate runtime is introduced.
+
+The supported first slice is authoring and structural validation. Cloth/FEM,
+strain-to-resistance evaluation, sensor dynamics, transient PCM and coupled thermal
+feedback are unsupported here. A product can derive its descriptive classification
+from connected domain facts; classification is not physical verification.
+
+Run the generic tests with:
+
+```bash
+python -m unittest tests.projects.test_layered_materials
+```
